# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# Get Medieval (KCD), 25 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames a mouse pointer move brings left out, the frame pool on a device of its own and its textures opened on the present's device (-wgcopen), 2026-10-14, build ab1772e; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 105.0 s to 1628.4 s
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description Get Medieval (KCD), 25 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames a mouse pointer move brings left out, the frame pool on a device of its own and its textures opened on the present's device (-wgcopen), 2026-10-14, build ab1772e; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 105.0 s to 1628.4 s
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 16
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.6
field_pull_wraps 18
#
# WHAT IT COVERS: the first of two streams of 2026-10-14, each from a relay launch of its own,
# 25 minutes cut to the gameplay its video shows, captured through Windows.Graphics.Capture with
# the mouse pointer in the picture, the frames a pointer move alone brings left out before the
# ring, and the frame pool on a device of its own whose textures the present opens through
# shared handles (-wgcopen). The arrivals are the game's pairs: 99.9% of the batches in the 60
# fps seconds are pairs, 0.14 ms apart at the median, with no single alone on the cadence, and
# the 155 seconds in which a pointer moved in a menu kept their 60 pairs a second. The policy is
# the one the tree ships. The game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 269 times an hour and stalled for 100
# ms or more 57 times an hour, in 37 bursts, 16 of them with a stall, and with no periodic
# stretch. The lock released twice: at 783.8 s, 0.63 s after a capture gap of 47 ms, for 2
# presents, and at 1607.1 s with no gap over 25 ms in the 3 s before, for 6. The worst blend
# run, 16 presents from 346.6 s, sits in a burst of 14 hitches and a stall of 266 ms (345.9 to
# 346.7 s). Of the 17 moves on the replay, 6 land more than 2 ms from a real frame.
#
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 45.655 s, from the 2691
# marked frames in its first 44 s, which sit within 0.38 ms of that offset (p90). The video runs
# 1582.7 s with no holes and stops at 1628.4 s of log time, where the stream lost its connection;
# the relay ran on to 2162 s, which no video shows. Its first 58.6 s are the main menu, the load
# list and a loading screen ending in a load stall at 104.26 s, so the cut starts at 105.0 s
# (video 59.3 s, gameplay after a fade from black) and the marked frames lie before it. Every
# second inside the cut that falls out of the 60 fps regime is a hitch second, 5 of them in 5
# runs, none longer than 1 s, so nothing was removed from the middle. The inventory and loot
# screens are inside the cut and in the regime.
#
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay reads synth 0.6% against 0.6% (0.6% and worst run 16 on the dejitter arm, which is how
# the stream ran), worst run 16 against 16, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and pull wraps 18 against 18.
# Counted over this window, blends are 527 against 527, repeats 254
# against 255, skips 56 against 56, and lock releases 2 against 2, each at the same moment. The
# replay makes 17 moves, 3 of them late, and the field's log has 17 in the window. The one
# repeat by which the two differ was not traced.
#
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
max_worst_run 16
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 1.0
min_reseeds 25
max_pull_wraps 18
extra_lag_ms 75
